  "surprise": "Mean 324 vs 081's 404: paired -68/-80/-92 on seeds 0/1/2, every seed worse; RL-solved 730 vs 854. Surprise: pretraining was unchanged or slightly better (steps 4772/4706/4737 vs 4682/4732/4769; final val loss 0.0930/0.0923/0.0944 vs 0.0950/0.0912/0.0964; held-out greedy 0.990/0.991/0.993 vs ~0.988), so cautious masking kept the loss fit but lost most of the RL benefit of strong Muon decay. This supports the preregistered countervailing mechanism: the 10x decay helps expert iteration through smaller or better-conditioned handoff weights, not through the pretraining loss, and skipping coordinates the gradient is growing acts like a weaker decay. Seed 0 started RL ahead (round-1 targets 254 vs 081's 187) but finished behind (807 vs 864); seeds 1/2 started low (168, 84). Weight norms were not logged, so the norm explanation is inferred, not measured. Total 980-1021 s, no timeout risk.",
